From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pet0203 <Pet0203@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8192-asurada: disable the SCP's
 cros-ec-rpmsg node

On google,spherion a mainline kernel hung on resume from suspend-to-RAM.
Two changes together made that go away; this is one of them, and the other
is "spi: mtk-nor: re-initialise the controller in runtime resume".

The node disabled here makes the SCP firmware's cros-ec interface appear as
a second ChromeOS EC device, reached over rpmsg. The machine's real embedded
controller sits on SPI (&spi1) and is untouched: keyboard, battery, charger,
USB-C policy and the EC's side of the suspend handshake keep working.

This is an empirical fix. Why the rpmsg instance upsets suspend/resume has
not been root-caused, and what else depends on the node was not
investigated: SCP-backed features such as the hardware video codecs were
not tested with or without it.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8192-asurada.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8192-asurada.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8192-asurada.dtsi
index 40d34b16d..0f4b95a67 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8192-asurada.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8192-asurada.dtsi
@@ -1386,6 +1386,12 @@
 	cros-ec-rpmsg {
 		compatible = "google,cros-ec-rpmsg";
 		mediatek,rpmsg-name = "cros-ec-rpmsg";
+		/*
+		 * The SCP's cros-ec interface. With it enabled, resume from
+		 * suspend-to-RAM hangs; the embedded controller proper is on
+		 * SPI (&spi1) and does not depend on it.
+		 */
+		status = "disabled";
 	};
 };
 
